# Flow-nav scenarios (Cancel / Back / menu)

Invariant: every wizard/submenu screen exposes **Отменить**, **« Назад**, or **menu Reply** (see `self_check/flow_nav.py`).

Map: [`docs/user-flow-map.ru.md`](docs/user-flow-map.ru.md) — backlog by §; not machine-readable.

## When this rule applies

New or changed **navigable UX**: screens, Reply/Inline keyboards, ConversationHandler steps, menu entries (`i18n.py`, `bot.py`, `handlers/`).

Skip: text-only prompt changes, internal refactor, §12 out-of-menu notifications.

## Required — ask the user

Before finishing the task, **ask explicitly** (do not add a scenario silently):

> Добавить сценарий в `checks_flow_nav.py` для §N (*кратко: какой экран*)?

- **§N** — номер раздела из `user-flow-map.ru.md` (или «новый §» если раздела ещё нет).
- If the user declines — note in the PR/commit message that nav check was skipped.
- If the user agrees — implement in the same change set and run `python -m self_check`.

Use AskQuestion or plain text when AskQuestion is unavailable.

## Where to implement

| Case | Where |
|------|--------|
| New/changed `ReplyKeyboardMarkup` / standalone inline keyboard in `i18n.py` | `_check_submenu_reply_keyboards` or `_check_inline_wizard_keyboards` |
| New handler entry / wizard step | New `_scenario_*` in `checks_flow_nav.py` using `_BotCapture` |
| Inline paired with `_pulse_wizard_keyboard` | Dynamic scenario; patch pulse → `cap.note_pulse()` or assert inline Cancel |

Copy patterns from existing `_scenario_subscriptions`, `_scenario_admin_broadcast`.

## UX fix vs test-only

If the scenario fails because the screen has no escape hatch — **fix the keyboard/handler first** (button or `_pulse_wizard_keyboard`), then add the test.

